[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etcd-io/etcd/issues/comments/148965712","html_url":"https://github.com/etcd-io/etcd/issues/3702#issuecomment-148965712","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etcd-io/etcd/issues/3702","id":148965712,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0ODk2NTcxMg==","user":{"login":"ark76r","id":7987921,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5ODc5MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7987921?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r","html_url":"https://github.com/ark76r","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ark76r/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-10-18T01:28:34Z","updated_at":"2015-10-18T01:28:34Z","body":"@yichengq \nI have no idea how to fix in without big changes in server API.\n\nThis is my preset user_auth.go file: https://gist.github.com/ark76r/21d880eb86d27642ab73\nAnd this is my test code: https://gist.github.com/ark76r/dfdf766b4425617ee2ba\n\nIn the modUser function I've added small code to dump actual answer from the server:\n\n```\nvar user User\n    dumpBody(string(body)) // <- here \n    err = json.Unmarshal(body, &user)\n```\n\nThis is the dumpBody:\n\n```\nfunc dumpBody(body string) {\n    pc, _, _, _ := runtime.Caller(2)\n    fmt.Println(runtime.FuncForPC(pc).Name())\n    fmt.Println(\">>>\", body)\n}\n```\n\nI've run my tests, and I've got among the other things such output:\n\n```\ngithub.com/coreos/etcd/client.(*httpAuthUserAPI).GetUser\n>>> {\"user\":\"userA\"}\n\ngithub.com/coreos/etcd/client.(*httpAuthUserAPI).GrantUser\n>>> {\"user\":\"userA\",\"roles\":[\"roleA\",\"roleB\"]}\n\ngithub.com/coreos/etcd/client.(*httpAuthUserAPI).GetUser\n>>> {\"user\":\"userA\",\"roles\":[{\"role\":\"roleA\",\"permissions\":{\"kv\":{\"read\":[\"/roleA/path1/*\",\"/roleA/path2/*\"],\"write\":[]}}},{\"role\":\"roleB\",\"permissions\":{\"kv\":{\"read\":null,\"write\":null}}}]}\n\ngithub.com/coreos/etcd/client.(*httpAuthUserAPI).RevokeUser\n>>> {\"user\":\"userA\",\"roles\":[\"roleA\"]}\n```\n\nIf I get it properly, server sometimes returns roles as a list of strings, and sometimes as a list of objects of type Role.\n\nThis is why we have to have two definitions of the user: \n\n```\ntype User struct {\nUser     string   `json:\"user\"`\nPassword string   `json:\"password,omitempty\"`\nRoles    []Role   `json:\"roles\"`\nGrant    []string `json:\"grant,omitempty\"`\nRevoke   []string `json:\"revoke,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\nand\n\n```\ntype User struct {\nUser     string   `json:\"user\"`\nPassword string   `json:\"password,omitempty\"`\nRoles    []string   `json:\"roles\"`\nGrant    []string `json:\"grant,omitempty\"`\nRevoke   []string `json:\"revoke,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\nAnd use first or second depending of the use case.\nIt's even more difficult, because almost all metods of interface AuthUserAPI jus delegate request to the function modUser and in this place I don't know what should I expect from the server.\n\nAnd this is why I belive server's API has design error.\n(of course it's 03:27am here, and I may be just to sleepy to see other solution)\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etcd-io/etcd/issues/comments/148965712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ark76r","id":7987921,"node_id